# AGENTS.md

Instructions for AI agents working on @@name@@. README.md explains the workflow to people; answer
workflow questions from it rather than inventing procedures.

## Language

Write everything in this repository (code comments, docs, journal, decisions, commit messages,
issues) in the language with tag `@@language@@`, whatever language the conversation uses.

## Session start

1. Read `docs/brief.md`, `docs/status.md`, the three most recent files in `journal/`, and the
   open issues (`gh issue list`, if available).
2. Run `uv run python .agents/skills/handoff/session.py uncovered`. If it reports commits or
   changes that no journal entry covers, draft the missing entry from `git log` and ask the user
   to confirm it before writing.
3. Work on one issue per session.

## Handoff

Propose a handoff (the `handoff` skill) when an issue is done, the user changes topic or ends the
session, or the context is getting heavy. The repository is the shared record; what is not
written there is lost to the next session.

## Skills

Skills live in `.agents/skills/`. Claude Code reads them through the `.claude/skills` link.

| Skill | Claude Code | Codex | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| handoff | `/handoff` | `$handoff` | end-of-session write-back |
| consolidate | `/consolidate` | `$consolidate` | merge the journal into `docs/status.md` (lead only) |
